<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A tea factory in Kericho has two machines, A and B. In a given month, the probability that machine A needs a repair is <m>{0.45}</m> and the probability that machine B needs a repair is <m>{0.4}</m>. These events are independent.</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find the probability that both machines need a repair.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find the probability that neither machine needs a repair.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Find the probability that machine A needs a repair and machine B does not.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The events are independent, so for <q>and</q> multiply the probabilities.</p><p>(a) <m>{0.45} \times {0.4} = {0.18}</m>.</p><p>(b) The probabilities that they do not happen are <m>1 - {0.45} = {0.55}</m> and <m>1 - {0.4} = {0.6}</m>. Neither: <m>{0.55} \times {0.6} = {0.33}</m>.</p><p>(c) The first happens and the second does not: <m>{0.45} \times {0.6} = {0.27}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{9}{50}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{33}{100}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{27}{100}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>